    "q-26137": {
      "dom_id": "step-q26137",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Let $(a,b)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $a+b?$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}0.4a-0.8b-1.2=0 \\\\ 0.5a-1.5b-5=0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply both equations by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}0.4a-0.8b-1.2=0 & |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 0.5a-1.5b-5=0 & |\\,\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}4a-8b-12=0 \\\\ 5a-15b-50=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we divide the first equation by $4$ and the second equation by $-5,$ we will get a $a$ term in the first equation that can cancel with the $-a$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4a-8b-12=0 & |\\,÷(4) \\\\ 5a-15b-50=0 & |\\,÷(-5)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}a-2b-3=0 \\\\ -a+3b+10=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $a$-variable and allows us to solve for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{a}-2b-3 & =0 \\\\ -\\cancel{a}+3b+10 & =0 \\\\ (-2b+3b)+(-3+10) & =0 \\\\ b+7 & =0 \\\\ b & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $b=-7$ into the equation $a-2b-3=0$ to solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a-2b-3 & =0 \\\\ a-2(-7)-3 & =0 \\\\ a+14-3 & =0 \\\\ a+11 & =0 \\\\ a & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-11$ and $b=-7.$ So, \n\n$$\na+b=-11+(-7)=-18.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
